From 27e419dc9f16d9f7898fa43e5ceda03ecacbfe1a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 05:46:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/18] KLZS (codec 31): the wave-4 KLZ stream format under its
 own id; rc3's KLZ (codec 28) kept

Ported from 0dc7a8b1 of the unmerged wave-4 LZ lane ("KLZ (codec 28): stream format
(literals, tokens, 16-bit offsets, extensions) and a decoder fast loop; 6-byte-key parse").
That commit replaced the codec 28 format in place: a frame written by rc3 with
KOLMO_NATIVE=lz in speed mode stopped decoding. Here:
- rc3's KLZ encoder and decoder stay as they were, under id 28 (kolmo_klz_*; its level
  table is KLZ0_LV, its window KLZ_WINDOW). Decoders keep reading rc3's frames; the
  opt-in no longer chooses 28.
- the lane's coder is kolmo_klzs_* under the new id 31 (C_KLZS); KOLMO_NATIVE=lz maps
  the LZ4 roles to it. An rc3 reader refuses such a frame.
- shared code as in the lane: kz_match (whole-register copies), the window as a
  parameter of kz_parse.
Tests: blocks written by the rc3 sources for codecs 28 and 29 (tests/klz_rc3_frames.h,
printed by tests/klz_rc3_emit.c built against rc3) must decode; the rc3 byte hashes of
both writers still hold; KLZS in the round-trip and corrupt-payload runs under ASan/UBSan.
natbench: klzs1..klzs3. Fuzz target: KLZS arm. SPEC rows for 28, 30, 31. Bindings synced.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FUEN4aRWhUw7yL7cZMqTmZ
